Something I didn't expect: a 2024 panel of 16 experts agreed screens hurt sleep in kids and teens, but reached no consensus for adults.

What seems to matter more is how late "one more" pushes your bedtime, and whether you put the phone down drowsy or wired. If you're wired, try six slow breaths: in for 4, out for 6.
